 ### Compile-Time Evaluation And Static Storage
 
+Structured embedding observations retain the checked module and compile-time
+root identities and that root's explicit CIR source. Cached observations replay
+with the same provenance from their checked root table. Literal-evaluation debug
+observations carry their checked source region and owning module instead. Hosts
+may use these identities to associate observations with requested notebook roots;
+message text is not an identity and must never be used to infer provenance.
+
 Frontend task completion and checked-value completion are distinct boundaries.
