 selected root requests before evaluating those roots. Importers may consume
@@ -2707,6 +2714,18 @@ the continuation reads, so target LIR lowering selects run/omit per consumer
 without any merge. Checked loop mutation and state merge plans likewise
 never look inside expect bodies, so both expect modes read the same plans.
 
+An embedding with a successfully checked frontend and a declared retained runtime
+consumer can inspect that consumer after constant crashes. The coordinator
+publishes an `EvaluationFailureSummary` while the typed evaluation problems still
+exist: its total error count and `comptime_crash` count establish whether crashes
+are the only finalization errors. The summary does not alter or discard any
+diagnostic, change a root's guardedness, or change ordinary command success. A
+failed constant keeps its producer-authored crash value; the consumer fails when
+it reads that value and may inspect independent roots. A mixed evaluation error,
+including a rejected conversion or exhaustiveness failure, does not permit this
+inspection. Frontend errors remain blocking and are checked separately before
+finalization; rendered diagnostic text is never used to establish these facts.
+
